    <div class="itdgl-pm-list" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
      <div class="itdgl-pm-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-pm-q">How to choose a performance marketing agency for a B2C brand brand in Hyderabad?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-pm-a">12-point evaluation framework: (1) Named B2C Brand (Generic)/B2C client work with verifiable case studies + live URLs. (2) Sub-vertical fit (correct sub-category expertise within B2C Brand (Generic)). (3) Ad-spend track record (Rs 1+ crore annual per client for scaling brands). (4) Attribution transparency (Meta CAPI + Google Enhanced Conversions + LTV/CAC/cohort). (5) Creative velocity (15-30 units/week Growth-tier, in-house pod). (6) Team + pod structure (dedicated senior on account). (7) Compliance familiarity (FSSAI (food/beverage), CDSCO (health/wellness), BIS (electronics/toys), ASCI (advertising) — India; ESMA + SFDA (GCC); UK CMA + trading standards + MHRA for wellness). (8) Multi-channel capability (Meta + Google + TikTok/Snapchat/YouTube + WhatsApp). (9) Reporting cadence (weekly + monthly + quarterly). (10) Founder + senior access. (11) Contract terms (6-month MSA with cancellation after month 3, 100% client IP, no ad-spend markup). (12) References + case studies from similar-stage brands.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-pm-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-pm-q">What is a realistic monthly retainer for a B2C brand performance marketing agency in Hyderabad?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-pm-a">In Hyderabad: Rs 75K-2.8 lakh (Starter to Enterprise). Starter (lower half): 1-2 paid channels + basic creative + monthly reporting for Rs 3-30 lakh/month revenue brands. Growth (mid half): Full-stack multi-channel + creative pod + WhatsApp + attribution + weekly reporting for Rs 30 lakh-3 crore/month revenue. Enterprise (upper half): Multi-region + celebrity/PR + advanced attribution + investor-grade reporting for Rs 3+ crore/month. Ad-spend separate + transparent pass-through: Rs 1.5-14 lakh/month typical.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-pm-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-pm-q">What ad-spend transparency should we insist on from an agency?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-pm-a">Transparent pass-through — client sees exactly what platforms bill (invoices, receipts, ad-account access). NO agency markup on ad spend (some agencies markup 15-30% hidden — massive red flag). Best-practice contract: (1) Ad-spend invoiced separately from agency retainer, (2) Client pays platforms directly OR agency bills exactly platform-invoice amount, (3) Full ad-account access for client + independent audit rights, (4) Weekly spend reports with platform receipts. For B2C Brand (Generic) brands, transparent pass-through is non-negotiable — bundled retainer + ad-spend usually hides 15-30% markup.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-pm-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-pm-q">What named B2C brand client work should agencies show?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-pm-a">Verifiable evidence: (1) Live URLs of B2C Brand (Generic) brand Shopify/website + Meta Ads Library + Instagram/social accounts. (2) 2-3 named client references (available on discovery call under NDA). (3) Case study PDFs with real metrics (revenue growth, CAC, LTV, ROAS, cohort retention). (4) Content library samples showing creative quality + brand voice fit. Reference brands to benchmark: Nykaa, Mamaearth, boAt, Noise, MyGlamm, Wow Skin Science, Cure.fit (India); Namshi + Ounass + Amazon.ae + Noon (GCC); Gymshark, boohooMAN, MyProtein, Made.com, Simba (UK). Red flag: 'we've worked with 50+ brands' with no named client work + no verifiable URLs = category tourism.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-pm-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-pm-q">What contract terms + exit clauses should we negotiate with a B2C brand agency?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-pm-a">6-month MSA (Master Service Agreement) with cancellation option after month 3 if agreed milestones not met — protects both sides. Ad-spend transparent pass-through — no markup. IP ownership 100% client on: creative assets, content library, ad account access, attribution setup, WhatsApp automation, customer data. Notice period 30-60 days. Non-solicitation clause reasonable. Avoid: 12-24 month lock-ins, IP-retention clauses, ad-spend markup, unclear termination terms.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-pm-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-pm-q">What team structure will an agency assign to a B2C brand brand in Hyderabad?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-pm-a">Growth-tier pod typical: (1) Account Director / Growth Lead — weekly review + monthly QBR + strategy. (2) Performance marketer(s) — Meta + Google + Shopping + PMax execution. (3) Creative pod — 2-3 designers + video editor + Reels producer (15-30 pieces/week). (4) Content writer — landing pages + email + WhatsApp + ad copy. (5) WhatsApp + retention specialist — Interakt/AiSensy + Klaviyo automation. (6) Local SEO + landing-page CRO specialist. Founder + senior partner on quarterly QBR. Enterprise adds: CMO/strategist + celebrity/PR + regional-market specialist.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-pm-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-pm-q">What reporting cadence to expect from a B2C brand performance marketing agency?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-pm-a">Weekly performance report: channel-level spend + ROAS + CAC + LTV/CAC + creative fatigue + attribution health. Monthly QBR (in-person for Hyderabad local + video for remote): full P&L review + cohort analysis + creative + audience + competitor + trend analysis + next-month plan + quarter forecast. Quarterly business review: revenue against annual plan + tier + channel + team + attribution audit + next-quarter strategy. Peak-season (Diwali + wedding + festive (India), Ramadan + Eid + DSF (GCC), Christmas + Black Friday + Cyber Monday + Boxing Day (UK)) daily reporting during peak weeks.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-pm-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-pm-q">In-house vs agency vs hybrid for a B2C brand brand in Hyderabad?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-pm-a">In-house makes sense at Rs 25+ crore/month revenue with 8-15 marketing specialists. Full agency for Rs 30 lakh-25 crore/month — access to specialist expertise + creative + tooling + compliance without hiring overhead. Hybrid (Rs 5-25 crore/month): CMO/Growth Head in-house + specialist agency execution. Bootstrapped brands: agency-dominant year 1-2, in-house Growth Head at Rs 60 lakh+/month, in-house team scales year 3+. In Hyderabad, most solo/early founders + 2-5 person marketing teams operate best with full agency for B2C Brand (Generic) brands.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-pm-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-pm-q">What are the biggest red flags in B2C brand agency proposals?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-pm-a">(1) 'Industries served: 20+' — category tourism with no B2C Brand (Generic) depth. (2) Guaranteed ROAS/CPL/lead-volume promises (unrealistic + often mathematically impossible). (3) Bundled ad-spend + retainer (hides 15-30% markup). (4) 12-24 month lock-in with no cancellation clause. (5) IP-retention on creative + attribution setup + customer data. (6) Junior-only team + no founder access. (7) No named B2C Brand (Generic) client work + no verifiable case studies. (8) Can't articulate Meta CAPI + Google Enhanced Conversions setup. (9) No creative in-house pod (outsourcing creative kills velocity). (10) Vanity metrics only (impressions + CTR + follower count, no revenue/CAC/LTV). (11) Weak compliance familiarity (FSSAI (food/beverage), CDSCO (health/wellness), BIS (electronics/toys), ASCI (advertising) — India; ESMA + SFDA (GCC); UK CMA + trading standards + MHRA for wellness). (12) English-only creative (excludes 40-70% of Hyderabad demographic).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-pm-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-pm-q">What is a realistic first-90-day plan from a B2C brand agency?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-pm-a">Month 1 — Audit + Foundation: brand + funnel + attribution + tech-stack + team + creative + compliance audit. LTV/CAC/repeat baseline. Competitor analysis. Attribution rebuild (Meta CAPI + Google Enhanced Conversions + WhatsApp CTWA). Creative + content pipeline design. WhatsApp Cloud API setup. First landing pages live. Month 2 — Launch + Iterate: paid campaigns live (Meta + Google + Shopping + PMax + Snapchat/TikTok if applicable). Creative testing 8-15 units/week. WhatsApp flows activated. First cohort measurement. Month 3 — Optimise + First QBR: channel + creative + audience optimisation. First quarterly QBR + 90-day performance review. Tier + budget recalibration. Quarter-2 plan. Milestones + go/no-go points at day 30, 60, 90. Cancellation clause after month 3.</div>
      </div>
